<header class="ws-head"><p class="ws-kicker">Worksheet &middot; Cultures</p><h1 class="ws-title">Worksheet: Cultures of Central &amp; East Asia</h1><p class="ws-lede">A worksheet on 14 cultures of Central &amp; East Asia, from the Jōmon culture to the Ainu. Read their profiles, then answer.</p><p class="ws-who" aria-hidden="true"><span>Name</span><span>Class</span><span>Date</span></p><p class="ws-tools"><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="0">Print the worksheet</button><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="1">Print with the answers</button><a href="/profiles?kind=culture&amp;region=Central%20%26%20East%20Asia">Open the cultures &rarr;</a></p></header>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Put the cultures in order</h2><p class="ws-how">Number the cultures from 1 (the earliest to begin) to 7 (the latest).</p><ul class="ws-order"><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Longshan culture</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Jōmon culture</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Yangshao culture</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Hongshan culture</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Liangzhu culture</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Erlitou culture</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Oxus civilisation</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Match the cultures to their homelands</h2><p class="ws-how">Write the number of the right homeland next to each culture. Their profiles will help.</p><div class="ws-match"><ol class="ws-ma" type="A"><li>Jōmon culture</li><li>Yangshao culture</li><li>Hongshan culture</li><li>Liangzhu culture</li><li>Longshan culture</li><li>Oxus civilisation</li></ol><ol class="ws-mb"><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>Southern Turkmenistan (the Kopet Dag foothills and Margiana in the Murghab delta), northern Afghanistan…</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>The West Liao river basin in northeast China, from Inner Mongolia to Liaoning</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>The middle reaches of the Yellow River in China, mainly Henan and the neighbouring provinces of Shaanxi and…</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>The Japanese archipelago from Hokkaido to Kyushu, with most people in Honshu and Kyushu</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>The middle and lower Yellow River valley of northern China</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>The Yangtze River Delta and the Taihu Lake area of eastern China, centred on Zhejiang</li></ol></div></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Think and discuss</h2><ol class="ws-qs"><li><p><b>Jōmon culture</b>. Its profile says: &#8220;For some 14,000 years the people of the Japanese archipelago lived mainly by hunting, gathering and fishing, yet many settled in villages, reaching a considerable degree of sedentism and cultural complexity.&#8221; Find one piece of evidence on the profile for this, and say how we know it.</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p><b>Yangshao culture</b>. Its profile says: &#8220;The Yangshao people farmed millet, and some rice, along the middle Yellow River and kept pigs and dogs; over two thousand years their region became a fully settled farming society.&#8221; Find one piece of evidence on the profile for this, and say how we know it.</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p><b>Hongshan culture</b>. Its profile says: &#8220;The Hongshan culture farmed millet in the West Liao river basin of northeast China from about 4700 to 2900 BCE; in its late phase millet made up as much as 80% of the diet.&#8221; Find one piece of evidence on the profile for this, and say how we know it.</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>Choose two of these cultures that lived at the same time. What did they have in common, and what set them apart?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li></ol></section>
<p class="ws-src">From The Epoch Institute: the-epoch-institute.org/profiles?kind=culture&amp;region=Central%20%26%20East%20Asia. Free to print and copy for use in class.</p>
<details class="ws-key" id="answers"><summary>Answer key</summary><div class="ws-key-b"><p class="ws-key-t">Answer key: Worksheet: Cultures of Central &amp; East Asia</p><section><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Put the cultures in order</h2><ol class="ws-key-list"><li>Jōmon culture <span>c. 14000 BCE – c. 300 BCE</span></li><li>Yangshao culture <span>c. 5000 BCE – c. 3000 BCE</span></li><li>Hongshan culture <span>c. 4700 BCE – c. 2900 BCE</span></li><li>Liangzhu culture <span>c. 3300 BCE – c. 2300 BCE</span></li><li>Longshan culture <span>c. 3000 BCE – c. 1900 BCE</span></li><li>Oxus civilisation <span>c. 2300 BCE – c. 1700 BCE</span></li><li>Erlitou culture <span>c. 1750 BCE – c. 1500 BCE</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Match the cultures to their homelands</h2><ol class="ws-key-list" type="A"><li>Jōmon culture <span>4: The Japanese archipelago from Hokkaido to Kyushu, with most people in Honshu and Kyushu</span></li><li>Yangshao culture <span>3: The middle reaches of the Yellow River in China, mainly Henan and the neighbouring provinces of Shaanxi and…</span></li><li>Hongshan culture <span>2: The West Liao river basin in northeast China, from Inner Mongolia to Liaoning</span></li><li>Liangzhu culture <span>6: The Yangtze River Delta and the Taihu Lake area of eastern China, centred on Zhejiang</span></li><li>Longshan culture <span>5: The middle and lower Yellow River valley of northern China</span></li><li>Oxus civilisation <span>1: Southern Turkmenistan (the Kopet Dag foothills and Margiana in the Murghab delta), northern Afghanistan…</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Think and discuss</h2><p class="ws-key-note">Open questions: answers will vary. Good answers use details from the profiles.</p></section></div></details>
